PX bond prices — FAQ and column definitions (build 2026-11-18f)
Basics
Where the prices come from. ALLREPO only: each repo row carries the bond leg in EUR (MTMSecurity_EUR) and the
bond face in EUR (NotionalBond_EUR). Price = |bond MtM| ÷ |face| × 100. No external price feed.
Dirty price. Includes accrued coupon: on a coupon date the price drops by the coupon with no market move.
FX. Both legs are converted to EUR at the same rate, so FX cancels in the price.
Rounding (LITE model). Bond MtM and face are stored to EUR 1k per row: prices are exact to about 0.01 pt on large
holdings; a small row can show steps that are rounding.
Sign convention. Same as market risk: repo MtM negative = in our favour. "+" in an effect = moves MtM against us.
Sides. 17A = repo (BuySell B): we delivered the bond, a price RISE is against us. 17B = reverse repo (BuySell S):
we hold the bond as collateral, a price FALL is against us.
Window. The PX window (1D / 1W / 2W / 1M / Custom). Start and end = the last ALLREPO file on or before each date.
Which trades count. Repo rows (07L), Sponsored per the PX switch. Prices and effects use trades started on the
file (forward-starting trades have no bond leg yet).
Assumption. 16A runs on the bank's booked prices (to confirm with market risk), so a wrong booked price is shown
as a possible cause of a 16A move, not cleaned away.